{"seq":16,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-company-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T16:28:16.515Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"360536e88efe35f1c901d803831db39da180d4527512d193f5503b8ba516f57d","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Found three QFL ticket numbers in Moss's notes. Here's the list for your weekly notes:\n\n1. #PD-4492: Eau Claire kiosk SMS bay assignments not reaching drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18. Patched 4 Oct 2025, confirmed by Thea 5 Oct. Source: teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md (\"Sunday prep for Ruth\", Moss). The same digest also asks for the Eau Claire kiosk logs to be archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n2. #4419: gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift, escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. Source: teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md (undated \"North cheat sheet\", Moss). The Q2 expansion wrap by Marcus (not Moss) also mentions #4419 as a Gate 3 printer lag, so the two descriptions may be different issues under one number. Worth checking with support.\n\nTwo Moss notes I checked had no QFL ticket numbers: the 14 Sep 2025 North pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in. The Central handoffs digest lists #4409 and #4412, but those belong to Central accounts, not QFL, so I left them out.\n\nI can't write to the weekly notes file, so this goes here for you to paste in. Tell me if you want it posted somewhere else."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
